{"step_index":1189,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:50:31Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-03T00:20:31+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-03T00:20:31+05:30\nShowing lines 10-30 of 272\n10: const GEMINI_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION = `You are a strict GST Invoice extractor. \n11: RULES FOR LINE ITEMS:\n12: - Extract items ONLY from the central itemized table bounded between the table header (S.No, Description, HSN, Qty, Rate, Amount) and the Subtotal row.\n13: - NEVER extract text from the header or footer as line items:\n14:   * DO NOT extract addresses or cities (e.g. 'Mumbai, Maharashtra').\n15:   * DO NOT extract PAN, GSTIN, or buyer details (e.g. 'PAN : 26CORPP').\n16:   * DO NOT extract bank account or payment details (e.g. 'Acc. Number 271').\n17: - Each valid line item MUST have a legitimate product name, quantity > 0, unit rate > 0, and total amount.\n18: \n19: GRAND TOTAL:\n20: - Extract the final payable Grand Total printed at the bottom of the bill (e.g., '4,490.00' / 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY'). Do NOT extract partial account numbers or phone numbers as the grand total.\n21: \n22: NUMERIC INSTRUCTIONS:\n23: - Never discard digits before commas! '2,535.00' must be extracted as '2,535.00'. '1,270.00' must be extracted as '1,270.00'. '4,490.00' must be extracted as '4,490.00'.\n24: - If you are unsure about the digits before the comma, read the 'Amount in Words' printed on the bill (e.g. 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY') to confirm the thousands digit.\n25: - All numbers and rates must be extracted as strings (e.g. \"2,535.00\", \"1\", \"4,490.00\").\n26: \n27: Return ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:\n28: {\n29:   \"vendor_name\": string or null,\n30:   \"gstin\": string or null,"}
{"step_index":1190,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:50:31Z","input_tokens":2957,"cache_read_tokens":32864,"output_tokens":1045,"tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"\"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/aiExtractor.js\"","Replacement":"\"const GEMINI_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION = `You are a strict GST Invoice extractor. \\nRULES FOR LINE ITEMS:\\n- Extract items ONLY from the central itemized table bounded between the table header (S.No, Description, HSN, Qty, Rate, Amount) and the Subtotal row.\\n- NEVER extract text from the header or footer as line items:\\n  * DO NOT extract addresses or cities (e.g. 'Mumbai, Maharashtra').\\n  * DO NOT extract PAN, GSTIN, or buyer details (e.g. 'PAN : 26CORPP').\\n  * DO NOT extract bank account or payment details (e.g. 'Acc. Number 271').\\n- Each valid line item MUST have a legitimate product name, quantity > 0, unit rate > 0, and total amount.\\n\\nGRAND TOTAL PARSING RULES:\\n- The Grand Total MUST be the overall final payable invoice amount, NOT a column entry, tax rate, or HSN fragment like '774'.\\n- Logic check: Grand Total must be approximately (Subtotal + Total Tax). \\n  Here, Subtotal is ~3,805 and IGST is ~684.90, so the Grand Total MUST be around 4,489.90 or 4,490.00.\\n- If you see a small number like '774', it is an HSN code, partial tax, or serial number. DO NOT use it as \\\\`declared_total\\\\`.\\n- Always look at the printed words: 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES' confirms the total is ~4,490.\\n\\nNUMERIC INSTRUCTIONS:\\n- Never discard digits before commas! '2,535.00' must be extracted as '2,535.00'. '1,270.00' must be extracted as '1,270.00'. '4,490.00' must be extracted as '4,490.00'.\\n- If you are unsure about the digits before the comma, read the 'Amount in Words' printed on the bill (e.g. 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY') to confirm the thousands digit.\\n- All numbers and rates must be extracted as strings (e.g. \\\"2,535.00\\\", \\\"1\\\", \\\"4,490.00\\\").\"","Target":"\"const GEMINI_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION = `You are a strict GST Invoice extractor. \\nRULES FOR LINE ITEMS:\\n- Extract items ONLY from the central itemized table bounded between the table header (S.No, Description, HSN, Qty, Rate, Amount) and the Subtotal row.\\n- NEVER extract text from the header or footer as line items:\\n  * DO NOT extract addresses or cities (e.g. 'Mumbai, Maharashtra').\\n  * DO NOT extract PAN, GSTIN, or buyer details (e.g. 'PAN : 26CORPP').\\n  * DO NOT extract bank account or payment details (e.g. 'Acc. Number 271').\\n- Each valid line item MUST have a legitimate product name, quantity > 0, unit rate > 0, and total amount.\\n\\nGRAND TOTAL:\\n- Extract the final payable Grand Total printed at the bottom of the bill (e.g., '4,490.00' / 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY'). Do NOT extract partial account numbers or phone numbers as the grand total.\\n\\nNUMERIC INSTRUCTIONS:\\n- Never discard digits before commas! '2,535.00' must be extracted as '2,535.00'. '1,270.00' must be extracted as '1,270.00'. '4,490.00' must be extracted as '4,490.00'.\\n- If you are unsure about the digits before the comma, read the 'Amount in Words' printed on the bill (e.g. 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY') to confirm the thousands digit.\\n- All numbers and rates must be extracted as strings (e.g. \\\"2,535.00\\\", \\\"1\\\", \\\"4,490.00\\\").\""}}]}
